.TH MACHINEPROXY 1 "2026-05-20" "MachineProxy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
machineproxy \- run a program locally while it operates on a remote machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B machineproxy
[\fIoptions\fR]
[\fIDESTINATION\fR]
[\fB\-\-\fR \fIprogram\fR [\fIargs\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B machineproxy
creates a mixed-reality environment: the target program runs on the local
workstation but every child process it spawns, and every file it accesses
through the mounted workspace, is transparently forwarded to a remote machine
over SSH or Docker.
.PP
The workspace directory is exposed to the target program via a FUSE/SFTP
mount.
Child processes are intercepted by a
.BR ptrace (2)-based
tracer (Linux) or a
.B DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
interposer (macOS) and relaunched on the remote machine via
.BR mproxy-agent .
File-descriptor inheritance and pipes work transparently across the
machine boundary.
.PP
This lets AI coding agents, editors, and other local-only tools operate on
machines that lack Internet access, cannot run modern runtimes, or must be
accessed from a different trust domain.
.SH DESTINATION
The destination selects the remote backend and target machine.
It may be a bare hostname (implying SSH), a
.IB user @ hostname
pair, or a scheme-prefixed URL.
.TP
.I hostname
.TQ
.IB user @ hostname
SSH backend.
Equivalent to
.BI ssh:// user @ hostname .
.TP
.BI ssh:// [user@] hostname [:port]
SSH backend with explicit user and/or port.
.TP
.BI docker:// container
Docker backend.
.I container
may be a container name or ID.
.TP
.BI compose:// project / service [/ id ]
Docker Compose backend.
Use
.B compose://./\fIservice\fR
to auto-detect the project from the current directory.
.I id
is the 1-based replica index for scaled services.
.PP
When no destination is given, machineproxy reads all connection details from
the configuration file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Path to the configuration file (TOML, YAML, or JSON format).
Default:
.IR /etc/machineproxy/machineproxy.toml .
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.BI \-backend " type"
Override the remote backend type.
Accepted values:
.BR ssh ,
.BR docker ,
.BR compose .
The destination URL scheme takes precedence when both are given.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-port " \fIport\fR"
Remote SSH port.
Overrides
.B remote.ssh.port
from the configuration file.
Only valid with the SSH backend.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-login " \fIuser\fR"
Remote SSH user.
Overrides
.B remote.ssh.user
from the configuration file.
Only valid with the SSH backend.
.TP
.BI \-os " os"
Remote machine OS (e.g.\&
.BR linux ,
.BR darwin ).
Used when selecting the
.B mproxy-agent
binary to upload.
Overrides
.BR remote.os .
.TP
.BI \-arch " arch"
Remote machine architecture (e.g.\&
.BR amd64 ,
.BR arm64 ).
Used when selecting the
.B mproxy-agent
binary to upload.
Overrides
.BR remote.arch .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-mount " [\fIlocal\fR:]\fIremote\fR"
Add a mount entry.
If
.I local
is omitted the same path is used on both machines.
Prepended before
.B container.mounts
from the configuration file.
May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-workdir " \fIdir\fR"
Working directory inside the container.
Overrides
.BR container.working_dir .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B machineproxy
reads a configuration file in TOML, YAML, or JSON format (default:
.IR /etc/machineproxy/machineproxy.toml ).
Command-line flags override the corresponding configuration keys.
An annotated example configuration is installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/machineproxy/examples/machineproxy.example.toml .
.PP
Key configuration sections:
.TP
.B [remote]
Backend type, SSH host/user/port, Docker container, Compose project/service,
and target OS/architecture.
.TP
.B [container]
Local commands whitelist
.RB ( local_commands ),
workspace mounts, working directory, environment variable filtering,
path-proxy mode, and file ownership translation.
.TP
.B [agent]
Environment variable filtering for the remote side.
.TP
.B [components]
Explicit paths to helper binaries
.RB ( mproxy-shim ,
.BR mproxy-tracer ,
.BR mproxy-agent ).
Auto-discovered from
.I /usr/lib/machineproxy/
when omitted.
.TP
.B [recording]
Optional session recording in MachineProxy wire format.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B machineproxy
exits with the exit code of the child
.IR program .
It exits with status
.B 1
if it encounters a fatal error before the program can start, printing a
diagnostic to standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MPROXY_*
Consumed internally by MachineProxy components.
Filtered from the container process by default.
.TP
.BR DOCKER_HOST ", " DOCKER_API_VERSION ", " DOCKER_TLS_VERIFY ", " DOCKER_CERT_PATH
Standard Docker client variables honored by the Docker and Compose backends.
.TP
.B DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES
Set by machineproxy on macOS to inject the exec-interposer library.
Stripped by system binaries compiled with the hardened runtime.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/machineproxy/machineproxy.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/machineproxy/mproxy-shim
Local shim that relays child process stdio to the remote agent.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/machineproxy/mproxy-tracer
.BR ptrace (2)-based
exec interceptor (Linux only).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/machineproxy/agent/\fIos\fR/\fIarch\fR/mproxy-agent
Remote agent binary, copied to the target machine at startup.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/machineproxy/examples/machineproxy.example.toml
Annotated configuration example.
.SH NOTES
.SS Linux Requirements
.B bubblewrap
and
.B fuse
must be installed.
On systems where unprivileged user namespaces are restricted (e.g.\&
Ubuntu with AppArmor), enable them:
.PP
.RS
.EX
echo "kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0" \\
    | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/80-machineproxy.conf
sudo sysctl -p /etc/sysctl.d/80-machineproxy.conf
.EE
.RE
.SS macOS Requirements
Install
.B macFUSE
(\fBbrew install \-\-cask macfuse\fR).
Most
.I /usr/bin
binaries are hardened and ignore
.BR DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES ;
they always run locally.
Install Homebrew equivalents for tools that must be forwarded to the remote.
.SS Security
Do not treat
.B machineproxy
as a security boundary.
The target program can execute commands on both the local and remote machines.
Only run programs you trust.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run
.B bash
with the current directory mirrored to a remote host:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cd /path/to/workspace
machineproxy remote.host \-\- bash
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use a non-default SSH port and user:
.PP
.RS
.EX
machineproxy \-p 2222 \-l admin remote.host \-\- bash
.EE
.RE
.PP
Attach to a Docker container, mapping a local directory:
.PP
.RS
.EX
machineproxy \-v "$(pwd):/workspace" docker://my-dev-box \-\- bash
.EE
.RE
.PP
Attach to a Docker Compose service in the current project:
.PP
.RS
.EX
machineproxy compose://./dev \-\- bash
.EE
.RE
